Ladybird reports “unable to capture screen” for a WebDriver screenshot
the compositor didn’t take, instead of a blank image. WebKit’s WebDriver
also reports it when its automation session fails a screenshot, mapping
ScreenshotError to UnableToCaptureScreen in CommandResult.cpp. Gecko’s
Marionette throws UnableToCaptureScreen instead of returning an empty
image when a screenshot’s dimensions come out empty, in takeScreenshot()
in MarionetteCommandsParent.sys.mjs. And chromedriver makes the error
from DevTools’ Page.captureScreenshot the command’s own, after one
retry, in ExecuteScreenshot() in window_commands.cc.
